      "Source URL: https://northcreek.nsd.org/fs/pages/2129\nCategory: enrollment\n\nNorthshore Enrollment Information\nNew student enrollment, including Kindergarten, for the 2026-27 school\nyear is now open.\nBy enrolling for the 2026-27 school year, there are a number of\nbenefits:\nConnection to your child’s school community including information about\nschool tours and Kindergarten events; and\nEarly enrollment helps the district correctly staff classrooms,\nservices, and prepare for great learning environments for our students.\nTo help get you to the correct enrollment form, please answer a couple\nof questions:\nNew families and current families have a different enrollment process.\nIf you have enrolled a student in the Northshore School District before:\nClick here if you have logged into parentvue before\nCLIck here if you have not logged into parentvue before\nIf you have never enrolled a student in the Northshore School District:\nClick here for instructions and to begin enrollment\nIf you need help enrolling your child or children for school, including\ntranslation or interpretation in another language, please contact your\nchild’s future school for enrollment information and support. You can\nfind each school's contact information\nhere\n. Your attendance area school is based on your home address. You can\nfind your child’s school by using the\nAddress Look Up Tool\n.\nIN-DISTRICT STUDENTS\nEach Northshore student is assigned to an attendance area school based\non their home address. You can find your child’s attendance area school\nby using the\nIf you would like your child to attend a school they are not assigned to\nwithin our district, a parent/guardian may fill out an in-district\nwaiver application. Please review the\nlist of schools\nthat are at capacity and unable to accept waivers at this time.\nNEW OUT OF DISTRICT FAMILIES\nMust submit a\nChoice Transfer Request\nIf Choice Transfer Request is approved:\nOut of district families must submit paper copies of\nenrollment forms\nand\nrequired documentation\nto the approved school.\nEnrollment forms -\nSpanish\n-\nPortuguese\nBelow is the timeline for the waiver waitlists, including\nout-of-district waivers.\nJanuary 6, 2026:\nEmployee Waivers (Grades K-12):\nAll Northshore School District employees continuing and new.\nCurrent In-district and Out of District Waivers (Grades K-12):\nStudents who are currently on an In-District or Out of District waiver.\nMarch 4, 2026:\nNew In-District (Grades K-12)\nStudents submitting a waiver request for the first time within the\nNorthshore School District service area. Includes students moving from\n5th to 6th grade and from 8th to 9th grade\nApril 2, 2026\nNew Out-of-District Waivers (Grades K-12):\nStudents submitting a waiver request for the first time out of the\nNorthshore School District service area.\nMore information regarding waiver forms, submission requirements, and\ncontact information for assistance are available on the\nNorthshore Waiver webpage\nWaiver Information and Frequently Asked Questions\nIn addition to excellent neighborhood schools, Northshore offers a\nvariety of choice schools and programs. A choice school or program may\nbe exactly what your child needs to thrive academically and socially. To\nlearn more about Northshore’s Choice School options, the application\nprocess, and tour or information dates visit our\nChoice School webpage\nChoice school applications for school year 2026-27 are now open\nEnrolling your student in preschool is a separate process.\nPlease visit our Early Childhood page\nfor more information for information.",
