    title: "School Supplies - Skyview Middle",
    content:
      'Source URL: https://northcreek.nsd.org/fs/pages/6211\nCategory: counseling\n\nSchool Supplies\nIn an effort to ensure equitable access to school supplies, reduce the\namount of money & time families spend purchasing items for school, and\npromote academic success for every student, the School Supply Advisory\nCommittee developed the following expectations:\nSchool supplies are requested but not required.\nTeachers may also request additional supplies for their individual\nclassrooms.\nItems marked with an asterisk(*) may be pooled into classroom resources\nfor all students.\nIf purchasing school supplies creates a financial hardship, please\ncontact our office manager, and supplies will be provided.\nExceptions to this list may be made for students in special educations\nprograms.\nWant to donate supplies? The Northshore Schools Foundations does a drive\nevery year.\nView this link\nfor details.\nSTUDENT SUPPLIES FOR 2026-27:\nArt & Ceramics\nEnglish Language Arts\nInstrumental Music\nMath\nPE Uniform\nScience\nSocial Studies\nFor 6th, 7th & 8th Grade Art and Ceramics classes we ask the students\nalso provide (in addition to the grade level recommended supplies):\nEraser\nSharpener\nWhite school glue\nWatercolor palette with brush (Basic student 8 - 10 color set like\nCrayola Washable Watercolors - Can be any brand. See sample below)\n6th Grade, 7th Grade, 8th Grade\nComposition notebook (wide or college ruled)\nColored pencils\nHighlighters\nSharpie\nPost-It Notes (large and small)\nHeadphones with a wire...no bluetooth headphones.\nSupplies:\nMethod Book:\nAll students are required to have a method book to use in class and for\npractice at home. These books are available for purchase online and at\narea music stores. Be sure to get the correct book for your instrument.\n6th Grade Band: Standard of Excellence, Comprehensive Band Method, Book\n1\n7th/8th Grade Band: Standard of Excellence for Bands: Essential Elements\nfor Band, Book 2\n6th Grade Orchestra: Essential Elements for Strings, Book 1\n7th/8th Grade Orchestras:\nEssential Elements for Strings, Book 2\nString Players:\nShoulder rest (violin and viola)\nClip on tuner\nExtra set of strings\nRock stop (doughnut) for cello/bass\nRosin\nCloth to wipe off rosin residue\nWoodwind Players:\nAt least 3 reeds in good playing condition. All clarinet and saxophone\nplayers should be playing on high quality reeds (i.e. Vandoren, Mitchell\nLurie)\nCork Grease\nA Swab/Cleaning Rod\nBrass Players:\nValve oil/slide cream or slide oil\nCleaning snake brush\nMutes as needed\nPercussionists:\nA pair of Vic Firth SD1 snare drum sticks and plastic bell mallets\nStick bag\nA percussion kit with bells and snare drum or practice pad\nAlgebra\n1 inch Binder or dedicated section in larger binder\nDividers\nNotebook Paper\nPencils & Erasers\nAlgebra 2/Trigonometry\nBinder\nPaper\nWriting utensil\nColored pencil\nGeometry\nNotebook/Composition Book\nColored Pencils\nMath 8\nnotebook\npaper\nwriting utensils\nPre-Algebra 1\nComposition notebook or spiral notebook\nPencils & erasers\nBinder (or dedicated section in larger binder)\nPre Algebra II\n1.5 in binder\nRuler\nQuad-Ruled Paper/ Graph Paper\nAt Skyview Middle School, all students are required to wear a uniform\nfor PE/Health-Fitness classes. Families have two options for purchasing\nuniforms. They can purchase a shirt and shorts from this link by August\n31st,\nhttps://www.companycasuals.com/SMSPEUniforms/start.jsp\nor buy a plain black pair of shorts, sweats or leggings and a plain grey\nshirt from another retailer. Students will write their first name and\nlast initial on the front of the t-shirt. The PE teachers prefer the\nprinted Skyview uniforms purchased from the link.\nThere is also an option to purchase sweatpants or a sweatshirt on the\nlink above. Those are optional and not required.\n*A reminder, all students attending Skyview will have a\nPE/Health-Fitness class during the year\n.\nPlease order by August 31st, so uniforms can be distributed as early as\npossible. All purchased items will be handed out by PE teachers during\nclass or at lunch.\nEmail Mr. Geller if you have questions: bgeller@nsd.org\n6th Grade\nComposition notebook -100 page, lined\nPencils - 24 pack\nColored pencils - 12-24 pack\nGlue sticks - 8 large\nSuggested\nScissors\nScotch tape\nPencil pouch\n7th Grade\nGlue stick\n8th grade\n1 3-ring binder, 2-3"\nBox of #2 pencils\n1 pencil pouch inside binder\n1 package of colored pencils\n1-2 erasers\n1 fine point Sharpie\n2-3 glue sticks\n3 colors of highlighters\nSmall, handheld pencil sharpener\n1 package of notebook paper\nUltra fine tip Sharpies\nBlack & dark blue pens\nPencils\nLined paper\nComposition notebook\nBox of pencils\nPackage of erasers\nFine point Sharpie\nOptional supply for 2nd semester: Cardboard Trifold Display - 36 in. X\n48 in.',
